  "conclusion": "No single driver explains the flagged month-to-month movement in the 2015 default rate. Across the 14 flagged-transition x dimension decompositions, mix (compositional, FICO-band or purpose) effects are small and dominate in only 0 of 14 cases (mean |mix effect| 0.082 pp vs. mean |rate effect| 0.769 pp): most of the movement is within-group default-rate change, not a shift in who applied. The model's own mean predicted PD moves in the same direction as the actual change every time but explains only a small share of its size, leaving most of each flagged change as residual - month-to-month noise in realized outcomes that the model's risk mix did not anticipate."
